## Verification BY NUMBER

### (1) Registration additive — PASS
`factory.demand.v1` (`demandRequestSchema`, src/observability/profile-demand-ingress.ts) kind union extended by ONE literal `promise-breach`; reason union by ONE literal `expired-immutable-deadline`; kind→reason map gains `"promise-breach": ["expired-immutable-deadline"]`. Source allowlist schema gains ONLY optional `promise_adoption_since` (aware-UTC regex, absent ⇒ source may not carry promise-breach — enforced at eligibility as `adoption-cutoff-missing`). The `inbox.publishDemand` RPC registration (src/daemon/observability-server.ts:596-600 → ProfileDemandService.publishDemand) is unchanged.
- Diff is purely additive: the ONLY modified existing line in ingress logic is the kind–reason map entry insertion; no union member, refusal or route removed.
- Legacy refusals verified still firing: `continuation-missing` ⇒ `route-proof-unavailable` (pre-existing test test/integration/profile-demand.test.ts:270-274 still green in my run); `successor-escalation` ⇒ `route-proof-unavailable`; `queue-claimable` still admitted; revision>1 ⇒ `continuation-proof-unavailable` (unit + integration both green).
- Demand still binds seatId===profileId (`owner-mismatch`), key route patterns unchanged.

### (2) Per-incident hashed IMMUTABLE receipt snapshots — PASS (experiment re-run)
`verifyDemandRef` (ingress) hashes the WHOLE FILE: `createHash("sha256").update(readFileSync(path)).digest("hex")` — the `selector` field never participates in the hash, so a selector cannot make a mutable ledger line immutable. demand-eligibility additionally REFUSES any non-single-receipt content at the same snapshotRef (`breach-receipt-unknown`), structurally foreclosing ledger/JSONL citations; `sourceRecordRef` (owned per-record snapshot) and (for derived waits) `censusRef` are each whole-file hash-verified against evidence roots.
- Header-file hash of the receipt == the snapshotRef.sha256 the demand carries; re-verified at publish AND lease (validateDemandRequest runs in both `publishDemand` and `evaluateLease`).
- **Append-stability experiment (mine, through the real provider + real receipt files):** receipt evaluated eligible → later unrelated append to the mutable source ledger (`promiseId: pr-next`) changes the ledger sha256 but leaves the receipt file BYTES UNCHANGED, file hash unchanged, and re-validation still eligible. The repo's own integration test does the same in-flow: append to `promises-ledger.jsonl` after publish, then lease succeeds. PASS.
- Post-publication mutation of the receipt itself breaks the whole-file hash at lease re-validation → `demand:invalid-event`, never silent re-binding (integration test, green).

### (3) Predicates — PASS
- Breach gate is ONLY: promise.status === "open" AND dueAt fully expired at observation AND now (`due < now && due < observedAt`). Closed/voided ⇒ `promise-already-resolved`; unexpired/exact-instant ⇒ `deadline-not-expired`; observation predating deadline ⇒ `deadline-not-expired`. (3 unit tests, green.)
- Derived waits ride ONLY the EXISTING read-only classifier, pinned by exact identity `factory.waits.reconcile@read-only-census` (exported constant), classification literal `live-past-due`, classifiedAt ≤ observedAt, censusRef hash-pinned inside evidence roots, and `due ≥ promise_adoption_since` (pre-adoption debt ⇒ `pre-adoption-debt`). Missing/foreign/stale classifier, census hash break, missing cutoff ⇒ refused. Armed promises must carry classifier null (`classifier-not-admitted`).
- NO dead-PID-only breach — unit test "never lets a dead PID found a breach": dead PID + UNEXPIRED deadline ⇒ `deadline-not-expired` (refused); dead PID + expired deadline ⇒ eligible (deadline alone gates). `liveness` is optional schema metadata, never consulted by any predicate.
- NO quiet/capacity inference — hostile probe against the REAL `DemandEligibilityProvider` (my probe, /private/tmp/breach267/out/probe-quiet-capacity.test.ts, 4/4 green):
  - quiet:true + unexpired deadline ⇒ `demand:breach-receipt-unknown` (quiet is not even representable in the receipt schema, additionalProperties:false)
  - capacityObserved {occupiedSlots:1, availableSlots:0} + unexpired deadline ⇒ `demand:breach-receipt-unknown`
  - bare quiet/capacity-only evidence ⇒ `demand:breach-receipt-unknown`
  Exact codes captured from the run: `quiet=demand:breach-receipt-unknown`, `capacity=demand:breach-receipt-unknown`, `bare=demand:breach-receipt-unknown`.

